1
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:28,125
♪♪

2
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,305
♪♪

3
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:51,443
♪♪

4
00:01:15,108 --> 00:01:18,101
♪♪

5
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:32,368
Okay, ladies and gentlemen,

6
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:34,337
all around us are
the soundstages

7
00:01:34,361 --> 00:01:38,141
where your favorite movie and
television shows are created.

8
00:01:38,165 --> 00:01:40,243
And right up ahead
there on Stage 15,

9
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:43,246
Catherine Welden
is currently filming.

10
00:01:45,172 --> 00:01:46,716
Here, Catherine, let me.

11
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,351
Come on.

12
00:01:48,375 --> 00:01:49,519
Ron, you know me.

13
00:01:49,543 --> 00:01:51,588
It's always better
if I do it myself.

14
00:01:51,612 --> 00:01:52,956
How's that boy of yours, huh?

15
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:54,023
Getting bigger?

16
00:01:54,047 --> 00:01:57,126
Oh, yeah, just
started high school.

17
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,662
That's great.

18
00:01:59,686 --> 00:02:02,732
As sweet as ever, Catherine.

19
00:02:02,756 --> 00:02:06,669
How did you get onto the lot
and into my dressing room?

20
00:02:06,693 --> 00:02:10,673
No "Hi, Peter, you look
great, I missed you"?

21
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:14,243
I'm about five minutes away
from shooting a commercial, Peter.

22
00:02:14,267 --> 00:02:16,212
For Catherine Welden Cosmetics?

23
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:18,381
What do you want?

24
00:02:18,405 --> 00:02:21,050
I saw your fourth-quarter sales
in the <i>Journal</i>... $12 million.

25
00:02:21,074 --> 00:02:23,953
I'm... I'm thrilled
for you, Katie.

26
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,756
Ron, would you tell
them I'll just be a minute?

27
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:27,757
Of course.

28
00:02:27,781 --> 00:02:28,758
Thank you.

29
00:02:28,782 --> 00:02:31,115
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

30
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,399
All right, why are you here?

31
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:38,167
I knew you'd want to see me.

32
00:02:38,191 --> 00:02:40,503
I mean, after all,
we were partners.

33
00:02:40,527 --> 00:02:42,372
Is that what you're
calling it these days?

34
00:02:42,396 --> 00:02:43,806
Of course.

35
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:46,342
We were living together when
we both came up with the idea

36
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:49,278
of creating a cosmetic
line in your name.

37
00:02:49,302 --> 00:02:51,547
You had nothing to do with that.

38
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,618
I think your memory's
a little vague.

39
00:02:55,642 --> 00:02:58,154
You weren't exactly
sober in those days.

40
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:00,556
So?

41
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:01,624
Are you threatening me?

42
00:03:01,648 --> 00:03:05,495
Catherine... your
secret is safe with me.

43
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:07,030
I'd never want anyone to know

44
00:03:07,054 --> 00:03:09,932
that you're a woman who drank
herself out of a movie career,

45
00:03:09,956 --> 00:03:13,236
disappeared from sight,
and then emerged sober

46
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:17,240
and beautiful with a
successful cosmetic line.

47
00:03:17,264 --> 00:03:19,542
If you think you're
getting a penny from me...

48
00:03:19,566 --> 00:03:20,677
I want half.

49
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:21,978
For what?

50
00:03:22,002 --> 00:03:23,513
Get out.

51
00:03:24,838 --> 00:03:27,950
Oh, my, my, my.

52
00:03:29,609 --> 00:03:34,557
Trust me, Katie, you don't
want me to take you to court.

53
00:03:34,581 --> 00:03:37,210
Katie, I've got great...

54
00:03:38,318 --> 00:03:40,096
Peter.

55
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:42,331
Hi, Jackie.

56
00:03:42,355 --> 00:03:43,966
How nice... your little
sister's still around

57
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:45,234
to pick up after you.

58
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:47,250
Get out of here!

59
00:03:48,762 --> 00:03:50,306
Think it over, Katie.

60
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:51,730
I'll be in touch.

61
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:56,727
What's he doing here?

62
00:04:03,777 --> 00:04:06,222
<i>Ben?</i>

63
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,257
Ben?

64
00:04:08,281 --> 00:04:09,772
Hi.

65
00:04:10,984 --> 00:04:14,797
Thousands and thousands
and thousands of dollars

66
00:04:14,821 --> 00:04:16,332
I'm gonna owe the
government this year,

67
00:04:16,356 --> 00:04:20,203
just thousands and
thousands and thousands.

68
00:04:20,227 --> 00:04:22,572
Why don't you let your
accountant sort that out?

69
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:25,875
These new tax laws, you
can't hardly write off anything...

70
00:04:25,899 --> 00:04:28,644
I mean <i>anything.</i>

71
00:04:28,668 --> 00:04:30,313
Why aren't you worried?

72
00:04:30,337 --> 00:04:33,816
I'm in a slightly
lower tax bracket.

73
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,418
You'd think I could
deduct something.

74
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:37,253
All I do is work.

75
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:38,688
Is this your way of telling me

76
00:04:38,712 --> 00:04:41,524
you're not coming
to Los Angeles?

77
00:04:41,548 --> 00:04:44,193
You going to Los Angeles?

78
00:04:44,217 --> 00:04:47,864
Ben, I told you I was going.

79
00:04:47,888 --> 00:04:48,931
Oh.

80
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:50,800
Aren't you coming?

81
00:04:50,824 --> 00:04:55,538
Oh, just thousands and
thousands and thousands of dollars.

82
00:04:55,562 --> 00:04:57,540
I wouldn't be any fun.

83
00:04:57,564 --> 00:05:01,811
Oh, my friend Jackie
is dying to meet you.

84
00:05:01,835 --> 00:05:06,716
Remember, I told you her
sister is Catherine Welden?

85
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:10,253
Oh, I know.

86
00:05:10,277 --> 00:05:14,090
I bet I've seen <i>The River
Runs Deep</i> six times.

87
00:05:14,114 --> 00:05:15,091
Well?

88
00:05:15,115 --> 00:05:18,194
I'm a huge Catherine Welden fan.

89
00:05:18,218 --> 00:05:20,210
Well?

90
00:05:22,222 --> 00:05:23,966
Oh, I just can't.

91
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,669
It's just thousands
and thousands

92
00:05:26,693 --> 00:05:29,539
and thousands and
thousands of dollars.

93
00:05:29,563 --> 00:05:31,274
- It's just...
- Okay, when I see her,

94
00:05:31,298 --> 00:05:34,210
I'm gonna tell her
you're a huge fan.

95
00:05:34,234 --> 00:05:36,078
Wait a minute.

96
00:05:36,102 --> 00:05:37,613
Yeah, this dinner for two

97
00:05:37,637 --> 00:05:39,282
at Renoir's... isn't
that wh... isn't that

98
00:05:39,306 --> 00:05:41,284
where I took you
after the Morgan trial?

99
00:05:41,308 --> 00:05:43,219
You can't deduct that.

100
00:05:43,243 --> 00:05:44,188
Why not?

101
00:05:44,212 --> 00:05:45,922
You took me there
for my birthday,

102
00:05:45,946 --> 00:05:48,324
and we didn't talk business.

103
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:50,860
Well, I was thinking about it.

104
00:05:50,884 --> 00:05:53,752
While you were holding my hand?

105
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:59,519
Well, they don't
have to know that.

106
00:06:03,230 --> 00:06:05,508
♪♪

107
00:06:22,649 --> 00:06:24,627
Truce?

108
00:06:24,651 --> 00:06:26,347
How nice.

109
00:06:27,587 --> 00:06:29,165
Katie, I'm delighted.

110
00:06:29,189 --> 00:06:30,714
Come in.

111
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:42,932
Looks familiar.

112
00:06:44,304 --> 00:06:46,170
It is familiar.

113
00:06:48,108 --> 00:06:51,135
Peter, please.

114
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:04,786
Drink?

115
00:07:14,567 --> 00:07:17,947
I came over to...

116
00:07:17,971 --> 00:07:21,384
After what happened
today... I was abrupt.

117
00:07:21,408 --> 00:07:23,152
I apologize.

118
00:07:23,176 --> 00:07:25,421
It's my fault; I
should have called.

119
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:28,090
I haven't forgotten how
close we once were,

120
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,593
so if you need money, I
would be more than happy

121
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:31,937
to help you.

122
00:07:35,922 --> 00:07:37,967
How generous of you, huh?

123
00:07:37,991 --> 00:07:39,969
You can't expect more, Peter.

124
00:07:39,993 --> 00:07:41,971
You want to know what I expect?

125
00:07:41,995 --> 00:07:43,964
I expect $4 million.

126
00:07:44,998 --> 00:07:47,576
Or what, you'll sue?

127
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,345
You had nothing to
do with my company.

128
00:07:49,369 --> 00:07:50,846
I'll walk into court

129
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:52,782
with pictures that will
make the front page

130
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:54,984
of the <i>National Informer.</i>

131
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:57,720
Remember how you looked
when we were living together?

132
00:07:57,744 --> 00:07:59,188
Drop dead!

133
00:08:00,547 --> 00:08:03,926
Not exactly the youthful,
glamorous image

134
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:05,361
your public has in mind

135
00:08:05,385 --> 00:08:07,363
when they buy Catherine
Welden Cosmetics

136
00:08:07,387 --> 00:08:11,334
expecting to look
exactly like you.

137
00:08:11,358 --> 00:08:13,869
Good-bye, image.

138
00:08:13,893 --> 00:08:16,419
Good-bye, profits.

139
00:08:25,905 --> 00:08:26,949
Thank you.

140
00:08:29,209 --> 00:08:32,254
Jackie!

141
00:08:35,615 --> 00:08:37,393
Oh, you are positively skinny.

142
00:08:37,417 --> 00:08:40,296
Oh, you don't look a day older.

143
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,320
You liar.

144
00:08:42,322 --> 00:08:43,299
- Oh!
- Come on in.

145
00:08:43,323 --> 00:08:44,323
Oh, are you okay?

146
00:08:49,496 --> 00:08:50,940
Remember how
embarrassed you were?

147
00:08:50,964 --> 00:08:52,408
Yes.

148
00:08:53,433 --> 00:08:54,867
Oh...

149
00:08:56,336 --> 00:08:57,747
Tell me about Ben.

150
00:08:57,771 --> 00:08:59,181
Is he cute?

151
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:00,649
Very cute.

152
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:03,419
Does he lavish you
with expensive gifts?

153
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:05,488
He's very cute.

154
00:09:09,816 --> 00:09:11,961
Oh, he's a big
fan of your sister's.

155
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:13,796
Who isn't?

156
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,765
So, what about you?

157
00:09:15,789 --> 00:09:20,169
What lucky guy is
sweeping you off your feet?

158
00:09:20,193 --> 00:09:24,874
Well, my last date
was, uh, let me see...

159
00:09:26,966 --> 00:09:30,664
about seven months
ago, this Saturday.

160
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:33,883
I think this is what
they call a "slump."

161
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:35,885
Oh, no!

162
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,553
Well, you need some fun.

163
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:40,089
Let's spend tomorrow together.

164
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:41,724
Ooh, I'd love that.

165
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:44,060
Oh... but first,

166
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:47,229
I have to listen to a
new ad agency pitch

167
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,465
and then interview
someone for a job.

168
00:09:49,489 --> 00:09:52,468
Oh, you're just so corporate.

169
00:09:52,492 --> 00:09:53,636
I know.

170
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:54,870
Isn't it great?

171
00:09:59,199 --> 00:10:01,710
<i>$12 million in national sales.</i>

172
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:03,479
Some might say
a staggering figure

173
00:10:03,503 --> 00:10:05,081
for a company only
two years young.

174
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:06,582
- The way it sounds.
- True.

175
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:09,919
I believe, however, that you
have just touched the surface.

176
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:11,087
Good.

177
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:13,055
- This sounds even better.
- I submit to you

178
00:10:13,079 --> 00:10:15,691
that this company
does not sell cosmetics.

179
00:10:15,715 --> 00:10:18,561
No, it sells your
image, Ms. Welden.

180
00:10:18,585 --> 00:10:18,904
Hmm.

181
00:10:18,928 --> 00:10:21,897
And that's what we propose
to do with our campaign.

182
00:10:21,921 --> 00:10:23,099
We are going to make

183
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:26,902
your products as sexy
as the woman herself.

184
00:10:26,926 --> 00:10:29,438
- I like that talk.
- I'll vouch for that.

185
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:32,174
Don't run to the bank just yet.

186
00:10:32,198 --> 00:10:33,742
What the hell are
you doing here?

187
00:10:33,766 --> 00:10:36,112
Edgar, your divorce
is working out so much

188
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:38,514
- better than your marriage.
- Someone call security, now!

189
00:10:38,538 --> 00:10:40,116
- Calm down. Calm down.
- Get him out of here!

190
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,118
I'm just making
a quick delivery.

191
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:46,021
I'm legally entitled to 30% of
Catherine Welden Cosmetics.

192
00:10:46,045 --> 00:10:47,323
What?!

193
00:10:47,347 --> 00:10:49,692
If I don't have $4
million by tomorrow,

194
00:10:49,716 --> 00:10:51,760
I'm suing this company,

195
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:53,629
and this will be Exhibit "A."

196
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,930
- You snake.
- What are you talking about?

197
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:56,365
Be interesting to see
what would happen

198
00:10:56,389 --> 00:10:59,869
to Catherine's image
and your investment

199
00:10:59,893 --> 00:11:01,704
if I dragged these
pictures into court.

200
00:11:01,728 --> 00:11:02,972
Oh, my God.

201
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:04,406
Never saw your ex-wife

202
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:05,741
like that before,
did you, Edgar?

203
00:11:05,765 --> 00:11:08,244
Edgar, please!

204
00:11:08,268 --> 00:11:10,613
It was a long time ago.

205
00:11:10,637 --> 00:11:13,082
Katie, all those fans who
idolize you... how do you

206
00:11:13,106 --> 00:11:14,383
think they'd feel

207
00:11:14,407 --> 00:11:17,987
seeing you drunk and
rolling around in bed with me?

208
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:20,071
Think about it.

209
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:54,456
Peter! Your door's open!

210
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:58,144
Peter, you left your door op...

211
00:12:10,163 --> 00:12:13,275
Oh, Julie! The police
think she killed Peter.

212
00:12:13,299 --> 00:12:14,977
And our attorney's out of town.

213
00:12:15,001 --> 00:12:16,879
Would you act as
counsel for Katie

214
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:18,414
while the police question her?

215
00:12:18,438 --> 00:12:19,982
Please?

216
00:12:20,006 --> 00:12:22,751
- Of course.
- Oh, thank you.

217
00:12:22,775 --> 00:12:25,054
So you recognize this
makeup bag, Miss Welden,

218
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:26,622
or any of its contents?

219
00:12:26,646 --> 00:12:27,623
Yes.

220
00:12:27,647 --> 00:12:29,158
So, it is your bag then, ma'am?

221
00:12:29,182 --> 00:12:30,893
- Yes, but I...
- Detective Stoner,

222
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:34,496
this makeup kit is
hardly sufficient grounds

223
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,865
for an indictment, no
matter whom it belongs to.

224
00:12:36,889 --> 00:12:38,968
Mr. Bates was in
the process of filing

225
00:12:38,992 --> 00:12:41,537
a multimillion-dollar
lawsuit against your client.

226
00:12:41,561 --> 00:12:43,072
And there was an eyewitness.

227
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:44,073
What?

228
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:45,608
That's impossible.

229
00:12:45,632 --> 00:12:47,076
A neighbor of the
victim's saw your car

230
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,478
leaving the murder
scene at exactly 6:30 p.m.

231
00:12:49,502 --> 00:12:51,146
- I wasn't anywhere...
- May, may I

232
00:12:51,170 --> 00:12:53,765
speak to Miss Welden for
a moment alone, please?

233
00:12:55,375 --> 00:12:56,809
Be my guest.

234
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:04,893
My God... What's
happening to me?

235
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:06,428
You're going to be
all right, Catherine.

236
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:07,763
We'll straighten this out.

237
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:11,800
I left that makeup kit
at Peter's last night.

238
00:13:11,824 --> 00:13:14,136
Julie, I didn't kill him.

239
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,537
I wasn't there tonight.

240
00:13:15,561 --> 00:13:17,539
Obviously, the
neighbor was mistaken,

241
00:13:17,563 --> 00:13:22,263
but I'm afraid that's enough
to file murder charges.

242
00:13:23,503 --> 00:13:28,350
Julie... What do I do?

243
00:13:28,374 --> 00:13:30,452
- Will you represent me?
- I'm...

244
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:32,988
a prosecuting
attorney, Catherine.

245
00:13:33,012 --> 00:13:35,491
You need a defense lawyer.

246
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:38,761
Well, then get me the best.

247
00:13:38,785 --> 00:13:41,130
And I mean the very best.

248
00:13:49,429 --> 00:13:51,106
H-Hello?

249
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:53,008
Oh, no, I woke you.

250
00:13:53,032 --> 00:13:54,243
I'm sorry.

251
00:13:54,267 --> 00:13:56,745
- Yeah, I was just...
- Sleeping?

252
00:13:56,769 --> 00:13:58,247
I know. I'm sorry.

253
00:13:58,271 --> 00:14:00,215
How are the taxes going?

254
00:14:00,239 --> 00:14:05,754
Oh, just thousands and
thousands and thousands of dollars.

255
00:14:05,778 --> 00:14:08,057
I, um, I saw Catherine Welden.

256
00:14:08,081 --> 00:14:10,259
What?

257
00:14:10,283 --> 00:14:12,728
I saw Catherine Welden.

258
00:14:12,752 --> 00:14:16,298
Oh, good. Did you
tell her I'm a big fan?

259
00:14:16,322 --> 00:14:20,089
Yes, I did, and she wants to
fly you out here to meet her.

260
00:14:21,828 --> 00:14:25,641
She wants to pay my
airplane fare to Los Angeles?

261
00:14:25,665 --> 00:14:28,210
Yes, she's very
anxious to talk with you,

262
00:14:28,234 --> 00:14:29,978
and I'd love to see you, too.

263
00:14:30,002 --> 00:14:33,916
Maybe I will. I'd get to
meet her and see you...

264
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:36,085
Maybe I can do
a little business.

265
00:14:36,109 --> 00:14:38,354
Make it a business trip.

266
00:14:38,378 --> 00:14:40,556
You know, deductible?

267
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:43,675
I think I can arrange that.

268
00:15:02,468 --> 00:15:04,613
<i>What did your
sister see in this jerk?</i>

269
00:15:04,637 --> 00:15:07,216
<i>Oh, what can I tell you, Ben?</i>

270
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,284
Peter was a
good-looking hustler.

271
00:15:09,308 --> 00:15:11,053
He took advantage

272
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:14,990
of Catherine at a very
low point in her life.

273
00:15:15,014 --> 00:15:17,359
She had gained a lot of
weight. She was drinking heavily.

274
00:15:17,383 --> 00:15:20,195
Y-You wouldn't have
even recognized her.

275
00:15:20,219 --> 00:15:21,897
Her career seemed to be over.

276
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,298
Hmm.

277
00:15:23,322 --> 00:15:27,102
Uh, why were these pictures
he took of her so important?

278
00:15:27,126 --> 00:15:28,971
Ben, Catherine became

279
00:15:28,995 --> 00:15:33,160
a star playing the loyal wife...
The good, beautiful woman.

280
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:36,111
That's her image.

281
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:40,315
These pictures are so awful.

282
00:15:40,339 --> 00:15:44,504
Well, they could destroy
her and our company.

283
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,359
Well...

284
00:15:50,383 --> 00:15:52,961
who else was at this
meeting when, uh,

285
00:15:52,985 --> 00:15:55,531
when this Peter came in?

286
00:15:55,555 --> 00:15:57,533
Well, aside from Katie and me,

287
00:15:57,557 --> 00:16:00,836
there was her personal
manager, Gil Altman,

288
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,137
and also Edgar.

289
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:04,006
Catherine's ex-husband.

290
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:06,108
Well, what was her
ex-husband doing there?

291
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:09,611
Well, Edgar and Katie have
remained very good friends.

292
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,447
Edgar's a brilliant businessman,

293
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:13,804
and he's the company's
financial advisor.

294
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:19,955
Oh, pretty soon, I'd better
go meet my new client.

295
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:23,959
Ben, I can't thank you enough
for coming out here so fast.

296
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:27,062
Now, I know why Julie's
been bragging about you.

297
00:16:27,086 --> 00:16:29,064
Yeah.

298
00:16:30,089 --> 00:16:31,633
So, you were bragging on me?

299
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,402
I told her you were cute.

300
00:16:33,426 --> 00:16:36,104
So, what do you think?

301
00:16:36,128 --> 00:16:37,739
I think I'm okay.

302
00:16:37,763 --> 00:16:39,675
I'm talking about the case.

303
00:16:39,699 --> 00:16:41,343
Oh.

304
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:44,546
Well, if I were Catherine
Welden's manager,

305
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:46,515
and my income were
tied to her company,

306
00:16:46,539 --> 00:16:48,417
those pictures would
make me very nervous.

307
00:16:48,441 --> 00:16:50,853
I'll go talk to Mr. Altman.

308
00:16:50,877 --> 00:16:53,388
- I'll fly Conrad out.
- Why?

309
00:16:53,412 --> 00:16:55,757
You know I'm going to
want to stay close to this.

310
00:16:55,781 --> 00:16:58,774
- Oh, I...
- Jackie and I are like sisters.

311
00:17:00,086 --> 00:17:03,818
Well, okay, but promise
me you'll be careful.

312
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:23,638
♪♪

313
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,842
Mr. Matlock!

314
00:17:46,866 --> 00:17:49,344
Ms. Welden.

315
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:53,482
Uh, I didn't know you were
in your, uh, uh... swimming.

316
00:17:53,506 --> 00:17:55,951
I-I can, uh... I can come back.

317
00:17:55,975 --> 00:17:58,654
First of all, my
friends call me Katie.

318
00:17:58,678 --> 00:18:00,989
- Oh.
- And secondly, I swim laps twice a day,

319
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:03,425
so you're gonna have to get
used to meeting by the pool.

320
00:18:03,449 --> 00:18:06,886
Oh, I, I could get used to that.

321
00:18:08,454 --> 00:18:10,399
Something wrong?

322
00:18:10,423 --> 00:18:11,900
You have a birthmark.

323
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:13,869
I've never noticed that
in any of your movies.

324
00:18:13,893 --> 00:18:15,304
Makeup.

325
00:18:15,328 --> 00:18:17,306
Oh!

326
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:18,440
Would you like some iced tea?

327
00:18:18,464 --> 00:18:23,631
Uh, yeah. Yeah. Ooh...

328
00:18:29,475 --> 00:18:34,198
- So...
- Well... Shall we get started?

329
00:18:35,815 --> 00:18:39,828
Yeah. Yeah, this, uh, um...

330
00:18:39,852 --> 00:18:43,732
Uh, th-this, uh, Peter
Bates, how did you meet him?

331
00:18:43,756 --> 00:18:47,102
My sister introduced
us, um, at a Lakers game.

332
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,870
She had season tickets.

333
00:18:48,894 --> 00:18:51,022
His seats were
right behind hers.

334
00:18:52,598 --> 00:18:53,909
I've seen pictures of him.

335
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:55,410
He was a nice-looking fellow.

336
00:18:55,434 --> 00:18:57,512
He was a hustler
looking for a meal ticket.

337
00:18:57,536 --> 00:19:01,817
Until I got sober, I didn't
see him for what he was.

338
00:19:01,841 --> 00:19:03,418
Well, you, you quit drinking.

339
00:19:03,442 --> 00:19:04,686
That's, that's the main...

340
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:06,989
main thing. Oh, yeah.

341
00:19:08,714 --> 00:19:13,495
Did he help you, uh,
create your cosmetics?

342
00:19:13,519 --> 00:19:15,631
Absolutely not.

343
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:19,501
Uh, why, why did you go visit
him the night before the murder?

344
00:19:19,525 --> 00:19:23,672
I thought if I offered him
<i>some</i> money, he might go away.

345
00:19:23,696 --> 00:19:25,774
Yeah.

346
00:19:25,798 --> 00:19:28,176
Th-That's when you
left your makeup kit?

347
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,479
Now, I know the
police have a witness

348
00:19:30,503 --> 00:19:33,382
who says she saw my
car the night of the murder.

349
00:19:33,406 --> 00:19:37,036
What I don't know is whether
she's lying or just mistaken.

350
00:19:38,077 --> 00:19:39,921
Yeah, yeah.

351
00:19:41,881 --> 00:19:44,026
- Now, Ben.
- Uh-huh?

352
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:45,627
May I call you Ben?

353
00:19:45,651 --> 00:19:47,129
Why, yes.

354
00:19:49,088 --> 00:19:51,600
Ben, uh, you know how
much I appreciate you

355
00:19:51,624 --> 00:19:53,235
coming out here to defend me.

356
00:19:53,259 --> 00:19:55,194
Oh, I, I wouldn't miss this.

357
00:19:56,595 --> 00:19:57,806
Would you mind?

358
00:19:57,830 --> 00:20:00,308
I'd like to... see
every document

359
00:20:00,332 --> 00:20:03,011
and hear about every phone
call that pertains to this case.

360
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:05,180
Would that be all right?

361
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,082
Why, yes, that
would be all right.

362
00:20:07,106 --> 00:20:08,917
That would be fine.
You'd be involved.

363
00:20:08,941 --> 00:20:11,386
Of course, I don't
want to be a pest.

364
00:20:11,410 --> 00:20:13,055
Oh, you couldn't be a pest.

365
00:20:13,079 --> 00:20:16,024
I mean, a mosquito's a pest,
and you're not a mosquito.

366
00:20:19,118 --> 00:20:21,496
Hmm. You have nice hair.

367
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:25,434
Oh, well... You
have nice hair, too.

368
00:20:25,458 --> 00:20:27,202
I'll, I'll, uh...

369
00:20:32,932 --> 00:20:34,409
Bye, Ben.

370
00:20:34,433 --> 00:20:37,079
Let me know if there's
anything I can do to help.

371
00:20:37,103 --> 00:20:39,095
Okay.

372
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:43,852
Aren't you going
to start the car?

373
00:20:43,876 --> 00:20:45,253
Oh!

374
00:20:54,653 --> 00:20:56,364
Thank you.

375
00:20:56,388 --> 00:20:58,633
Ms. March, please come in.

376
00:20:58,657 --> 00:21:00,435
Hello, Mr. Altman.

377
00:21:00,459 --> 00:21:03,538
I really appreciate your
seeing me on such short notice.

378
00:21:03,562 --> 00:21:05,173
Not at all. I just
want to help Katie.

379
00:21:05,197 --> 00:21:07,342
Please, sit down.

380
00:21:07,366 --> 00:21:10,579
My goodness... you certainly
know a lot of celebrities.

381
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:12,881
Well, I've been in
the biz for 20 years.

382
00:21:12,905 --> 00:21:16,418
And, uh, I understand
that right now

383
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:18,620
Catherine is your only client.

384
00:21:18,644 --> 00:21:22,513
Well, Katie's career is,
uh, certainly a handful.

385
00:21:25,417 --> 00:21:26,661
Aren't those the, um,

386
00:21:26,685 --> 00:21:30,432
photographs of Catherine
that, uh, Peter gave you?

387
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,334
Yes, they are.

388
00:21:32,358 --> 00:21:35,237
I saw them.

389
00:21:35,261 --> 00:21:38,006
Catherine Welden.

390
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:39,965
Every man's dream.

391
00:21:41,934 --> 00:21:43,732
Shocked the hell out of me.

392
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:49,885
Well, no one else
is going to see these.

393
00:21:49,909 --> 00:21:51,887
I hope not.

394
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:54,022
If those photographs
were made public,

395
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:56,558
it would ruin both of you.

396
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:58,593
- Both of us?
- Oh, yes.

397
00:21:58,617 --> 00:22:01,429
Catherine's image is
what gets her acting roles

398
00:22:01,453 --> 00:22:05,652
and sells her makeup
and pays your mortgage...

399
00:22:06,692 --> 00:22:08,069
You know, Ms. March,

400
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:11,907
people think agents and
managers in this town are bad.

401
00:22:11,931 --> 00:22:15,110
But, uh, not that bad.

402
00:22:15,134 --> 00:22:17,512
Now, don't you think it
would have been stupid of me

403
00:22:17,536 --> 00:22:19,714
to kill Peter and
frame my client?

404
00:22:19,738 --> 00:22:23,084
I mean, isn't that kind of like,
uh, shooting myself in the foot?

405
00:22:23,108 --> 00:22:25,787
I don't think
Catherine was framed.

406
00:22:43,896 --> 00:22:45,607
Who are these people?

407
00:22:45,631 --> 00:22:47,509
The couples I had at
my house for a barbecue

408
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:49,678
the night Peter was killed.

409
00:22:49,702 --> 00:22:53,036
Just in case you want
to verify my whereabouts.

410
00:23:01,013 --> 00:23:02,224
That looks delicious.

411
00:23:02,248 --> 00:23:04,726
- Well, it is.
- Yeah?

412
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:08,964
Well, I've got to tell you,
I have never heard a wife

413
00:23:08,988 --> 00:23:12,550
speak so highly of
her ex-husband, ever.

414
00:23:14,326 --> 00:23:15,937
Well, I adore Katie, too.

415
00:23:15,961 --> 00:23:18,206
And I've got to hand it to you,

416
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:22,410
most men wouldn't look after
their wives' business affairs,

417
00:23:22,434 --> 00:23:24,699
uh, after the divorce.

418
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:29,117
Well... our, uh, our
marriage is over,

419
00:23:29,141 --> 00:23:31,152
but our friendship isn't.

420
00:23:31,176 --> 00:23:32,838
Besides, I own a
piece of the company.

421
00:23:34,513 --> 00:23:36,157
- Uh...
- May I bring you something?

422
00:23:36,181 --> 00:23:37,911
Yes, some soup... anything.

423
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:41,663
I bet you hated it when, uh,

424
00:23:41,687 --> 00:23:44,332
Catherine left with
that, uh, Peter Bates.

425
00:23:44,356 --> 00:23:48,370
Broke my heart to
see her with that creep.

426
00:23:48,394 --> 00:23:50,572
How long did she live with him?

427
00:23:50,596 --> 00:23:52,974
What... year, year and a half.

428
00:23:52,998 --> 00:23:55,043
Didn't you try to stop her?

429
00:23:55,067 --> 00:23:58,046
Well... she wouldn't listen.

430
00:23:58,070 --> 00:24:01,383
See, her career was
in trouble. She'd, uh...

431
00:24:01,407 --> 00:24:03,285
Well, she started drinking.

432
00:24:03,309 --> 00:24:05,553
And he made her feel young.

433
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:10,792
See, beautiful
women, like Catherine...

434
00:24:10,816 --> 00:24:13,650
they know that beauty won't
last, and it terrifies them.

435
00:24:15,988 --> 00:24:19,425
In a way, that... that
face is her curse.

436
00:24:20,993 --> 00:24:23,905
I know a lot of women who'd
like to be cursed like that.

437
00:24:25,931 --> 00:24:28,127
Oh... thank you.

438
00:24:30,002 --> 00:24:33,214
I bet you could have
cheerfully wrung his neck

439
00:24:33,238 --> 00:24:36,367
when he walked in there with
those pictures of Catherine.

440
00:24:39,511 --> 00:24:41,890
You're all right,
Mr. Matlock, you know that?

441
00:24:41,914 --> 00:24:44,213
- You know what I mean.
- Yeah.

442
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,331
What is that you're having?

443
00:24:49,355 --> 00:24:52,018
- Steak and mushrooms.
- Hmm.

444
00:24:53,625 --> 00:24:55,617
You want a bite?

445
00:24:56,862 --> 00:24:58,728
Um, well...

446
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:04,259
Mmm...

447
00:25:05,804 --> 00:25:08,350
You'd like to know where I
was that night, wouldn't you?

448
00:25:08,374 --> 00:25:09,584
I wouldn't mind.

449
00:25:09,608 --> 00:25:12,420
Well, I was in there,
losing my shirt...

450
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:14,456
playing bridge, all night long.

451
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,472
Hmm...

452
00:25:21,754 --> 00:25:22,915
Oh...

453
00:25:25,891 --> 00:25:29,157
Mmm... mmm.

454
00:26:20,446 --> 00:26:22,457
Thank you.

455
00:26:31,323 --> 00:26:32,985
What's wrong?

456
00:26:34,159 --> 00:26:36,037
What is it?

457
00:26:36,061 --> 00:26:41,142
Well... I found a letter
over at Peter Bates' house.

458
00:26:41,166 --> 00:26:42,977
What kind of a letter?

459
00:26:43,001 --> 00:26:44,993
A love letter.

460
00:26:46,505 --> 00:26:48,483
Poor Catherine...

461
00:26:48,507 --> 00:26:50,318
What Peter put her through.

462
00:26:50,342 --> 00:26:53,176
It wasn't from her.
It was from Jackie.

463
00:26:55,948 --> 00:27:01,996
Jackie... Flemming wrote
a love letter to Peter?

464
00:27:02,020 --> 00:27:05,533
She was the one who
introduced Catherine to him.

465
00:27:05,557 --> 00:27:07,602
Jackie Flemming
was in love with Peter,

466
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:09,527
and she never told me?!

467
00:27:11,530 --> 00:27:13,522
Oh, don't do that.

468
00:27:17,002 --> 00:27:21,116
Jackie... didn't kill Peter.

469
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:22,450
You can't be sure.

470
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:24,819
Yes, I am.

471
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:26,521
She didn't.

472
00:27:26,545 --> 00:27:28,790
Well, I'm going to have
to talk with her, anyway.

473
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:31,126
No, uh, I'll talk to her.

474
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:34,086
She... she tells me everything.

475
00:27:36,822 --> 00:27:38,814
Except about Peter.

476
00:27:49,401 --> 00:27:52,080
No doubt about
it, Ben is adorable.

477
00:27:52,104 --> 00:27:54,682
Ah, it must be his white hair.

478
00:27:54,706 --> 00:27:57,485
So distinguished.

479
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:59,487
And he's so real.

480
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:04,359
Most L.A. lawyers
are so plastic.

481
00:28:04,383 --> 00:28:08,096
You've got to get
him to move to L.A.

482
00:28:08,120 --> 00:28:10,131
He'll make a fortune.
Then you'll get married

483
00:28:10,155 --> 00:28:12,000
and you and I can see
each other every day...

484
00:28:12,024 --> 00:28:15,517
Why didn't you tell me about
your relationship with Peter?

485
00:28:17,896 --> 00:28:21,409
Ben found a letter you wrote
to Peter three years ago.

486
00:28:21,433 --> 00:28:23,834
You were in love
with him, Jackie.

487
00:28:31,977 --> 00:28:36,357
I, uh... I never
lied to you, Julie.

488
00:28:36,381 --> 00:28:39,661
You know that Peter had
season basketball tickets

489
00:28:39,685 --> 00:28:41,162
in the row behind mine.

490
00:28:41,186 --> 00:28:43,798
Catherine mentioned that to Ben.

491
00:28:43,822 --> 00:28:46,901
And we struck up an acquaintance

492
00:28:46,925 --> 00:28:49,337
and then a friendship...

493
00:28:49,361 --> 00:28:51,439
And then we began dating.

494
00:28:51,463 --> 00:28:53,274
Was he interested in you?

495
00:28:53,298 --> 00:28:54,309
Only as a friend.

496
00:28:54,333 --> 00:28:56,811
We never even kissed.

497
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,997
Then why did you
write that letter?

498
00:29:02,674 --> 00:29:06,654
Because as good
as I am in business,

499
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:09,170
that's how bad I am about men.

500
00:29:10,782 --> 00:29:12,927
A man pays a
little attention to me

501
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:15,663
and I fall head over
heels in two minutes.

502
00:29:15,687 --> 00:29:17,999
Does Catherine
know you dated Peter?

503
00:29:18,023 --> 00:29:20,101
- No!
- Oh, Jackie, why...

504
00:29:20,125 --> 00:29:23,905
why didn't you just tell her
that you had feelings for him?

505
00:29:23,929 --> 00:29:26,808
Because he didn't share them.

506
00:29:26,832 --> 00:29:30,478
That romance happened so fast.

507
00:29:30,502 --> 00:29:33,615
Ten days after I
introduced them,

508
00:29:33,639 --> 00:29:35,631
Peter moved in with Catherine.

509
00:29:37,476 --> 00:29:39,654
And she was crazy about him.

510
00:29:39,678 --> 00:29:41,356
And so were you?

511
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:42,712
Oh, yeah.

512
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:47,149
I just couldn't tell her.

513
00:29:48,186 --> 00:29:50,365
Not even after she left Peter?

514
00:29:50,389 --> 00:29:53,368
I didn't want her to know
how messed-up I had gotten

515
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:57,090
over a guy who
turned out to be a bum.

516
00:29:59,498 --> 00:30:01,660
You want to know the worst part?

517
00:30:03,335 --> 00:30:05,980
Now that I think about it,

518
00:30:06,004 --> 00:30:09,984
I'm convinced that Peter
struck up a friendship with me

519
00:30:10,008 --> 00:30:11,986
so he could meet Katie.

520
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:14,555
Jackie, do you know
how this could look

521
00:30:14,579 --> 00:30:16,557
to people who don't know you?

522
00:30:16,581 --> 00:30:19,527
Julie, do you know
where I was that night?

523
00:30:19,551 --> 00:30:22,430
In my office, in a meeting.

524
00:30:22,454 --> 00:30:25,333
That's the truth.

525
00:30:25,357 --> 00:30:27,690
You must believe me.

526
00:30:36,702 --> 00:30:38,546
Ben, thanks for
coming over so fast.

527
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:39,547
Oh, yeah.

528
00:30:39,571 --> 00:30:40,915
Come over here.

529
00:30:40,939 --> 00:30:42,216
I want to show you
something I found

530
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:44,285
- in this police report.
- Okay.

531
00:30:44,309 --> 00:30:46,954
I found something. I don't
know whether it means anything.

532
00:30:48,780 --> 00:30:50,258
What?

533
00:30:50,282 --> 00:30:54,162
Boy, you, you're really
hands-on on this, aren't you?

534
00:30:54,186 --> 00:30:56,097
Well, Ben, when I left Peter,

535
00:30:56,121 --> 00:30:58,132
it came down to
me making a choice.

536
00:30:58,156 --> 00:31:00,835
I could be one of those
actresses you read about

537
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:04,072
that wallow in self-pity when
their career slows down, or...

538
00:31:04,096 --> 00:31:06,307
I could take
responsibility for my life.

539
00:31:06,331 --> 00:31:07,608
You're a fighter.

540
00:31:07,632 --> 00:31:08,710
Oh, yeah.

541
00:31:08,734 --> 00:31:10,345
So, what'd you find?

542
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:12,814
Right here... the makeup
kit I left at Peter's...

543
00:31:12,838 --> 00:31:14,949
- The police list six items.
- Yeah?

544
00:31:14,973 --> 00:31:16,484
Well, a concealer's missing.

545
00:31:16,508 --> 00:31:18,219
There should be
seven items in this kit.

546
00:31:18,243 --> 00:31:19,721
Are you sure?

547
00:31:19,745 --> 00:31:22,123
I'm positive.

548
00:31:22,147 --> 00:31:24,639
Well, why would someone
steal your makeup?

549
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,337
Ms. March. Hi.

550
00:31:36,361 --> 00:31:37,505
Hi, Faith.

551
00:31:37,529 --> 00:31:38,639
I'm sorry. Miss
Flemming isn't in.

552
00:31:38,663 --> 00:31:40,942
Actually, I wanted
to talk to you.

553
00:31:40,966 --> 00:31:42,677
Sure, what about?

554
00:31:42,701 --> 00:31:45,246
Well, you know that
I'm helping Mr. Matlock

555
00:31:45,270 --> 00:31:47,215
investigate Peter Bates' murder.

556
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:49,617
Oh. I didn't really know him.

557
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:50,685
I know that.

558
00:31:50,709 --> 00:31:53,054
But on the night he was killed,

559
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:55,056
Miss Flemming
interviewed a man named...

560
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:58,025
Ken Evans.

561
00:31:58,049 --> 00:31:59,727
Did Mr. Evans kill...?

562
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:00,862
Oh, no. No, no, no.

563
00:32:00,886 --> 00:32:03,331
I just need to know
where everybody was.

564
00:32:03,355 --> 00:32:06,234
Now, the meeting was at 6:00?

565
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:07,869
Well, it was
supposed to be at 6:00.

566
00:32:07,893 --> 00:32:09,570
It wasn't?

567
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,372
Well, Mr. Evans called
and said he had car trouble,

568
00:32:11,396 --> 00:32:13,241
and Miss Flemming
asked me to go pick him up.

569
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:15,843
How long were you gone?

570
00:32:15,867 --> 00:32:18,063
Almost an hour.

571
00:32:22,574 --> 00:32:24,018
<i>Detective Stoner...</i>

572
00:32:24,042 --> 00:32:28,189
did you find any evidence of
Catherine Welden's presence

573
00:32:28,213 --> 00:32:30,491
at Peter Bates' house
on the night of the murder?

574
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:32,827
Yes, sir, I did.

575
00:32:32,851 --> 00:32:35,329
I'd like to show you
People's Exhibit 27...

576
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:36,631
This makeup kit...

577
00:32:36,655 --> 00:32:38,733
And ask if you can identify it.

578
00:32:38,757 --> 00:32:40,067
This has my mark.

579
00:32:40,091 --> 00:32:42,703
I found this makeup kit
in Mr. Bates' living room.

580
00:32:42,727 --> 00:32:43,805
Did you discover who owns it?

581
00:32:43,829 --> 00:32:44,839
Yes, sir, we did.

582
00:32:44,863 --> 00:32:46,707
See, that kit looks exactly like

583
00:32:46,731 --> 00:32:48,709
every other makeup kit
sold throughout the city

584
00:32:48,733 --> 00:32:50,344
by the Catherine Welden
Cosmetic Company.

585
00:32:50,368 --> 00:32:52,079
- Uh-huh?
- But there's one difference.

586
00:32:52,103 --> 00:32:53,881
The regular kits
that are sold at retail

587
00:32:53,905 --> 00:32:56,150
have plastic tops
that are painted gold.

588
00:32:56,174 --> 00:32:59,220
This kit has solid gold tops.

589
00:32:59,244 --> 00:33:02,190
There was only one
specifically made that way.

590
00:33:02,214 --> 00:33:04,292
And who was this made for?

591
00:33:04,316 --> 00:33:05,993
Catherine Welden.

592
00:33:06,017 --> 00:33:08,763
She's the only one that has a
makeup kit with solid gold tops.

593
00:33:08,787 --> 00:33:10,264
Thank you.

594
00:33:10,288 --> 00:33:12,233
No further questions,
Your Honor.

595
00:33:12,257 --> 00:33:13,935
Your witness, Mr. Matlock.

596
00:33:13,959 --> 00:33:15,336
Thank you.

597
00:33:16,361 --> 00:33:19,640
Uh, Detective Stoner...

598
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:22,710
uh... there's no real way

599
00:33:22,734 --> 00:33:26,614
of telling when this
makeup kit was left

600
00:33:26,638 --> 00:33:30,017
at, uh, Mr. Bates's
house, is there?

601
00:33:30,041 --> 00:33:31,352
No, not really.

602
00:33:31,376 --> 00:33:33,488
It could have been
left there a month ago

603
00:33:33,512 --> 00:33:34,655
or a week ago

604
00:33:34,679 --> 00:33:37,692
or the night before
Mr. Bates was murdered.

605
00:33:37,716 --> 00:33:38,826
Couldn't it?

606
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:39,961
Yes.

607
00:33:39,985 --> 00:33:40,995
And my client

608
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:44,832
told you that she
left this makeup kit

609
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:48,169
at Mr. Bates's house the
night before the murder.

610
00:33:48,193 --> 00:33:51,839
She had brought Mr. Bates
a gift, a kind of peace offering.

611
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:53,107
- Right?
- Yeah.

612
00:33:53,131 --> 00:33:55,810
She said something
about a crystal elephant.

613
00:33:55,834 --> 00:33:58,145
Which makes no sense, since
no such elephant was found

614
00:33:58,169 --> 00:33:59,413
on the premises.

615
00:33:59,437 --> 00:34:01,182
Your Honor, would
you instruct the witness

616
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:03,784
to just answer my questions
without editorializing?

617
00:34:07,012 --> 00:34:09,357
Detective Stoner, you've
appeared in my courtroom before.

618
00:34:09,381 --> 00:34:10,825
You know better than that.

619
00:34:12,150 --> 00:34:15,096
Excuse me, Your Honor.

620
00:34:19,591 --> 00:34:21,502
Ask for a recess.

621
00:34:21,526 --> 00:34:22,503
What?

622
00:34:22,527 --> 00:34:24,405
Ask for a recess.

623
00:34:24,429 --> 00:34:25,406
Why?

624
00:34:25,430 --> 00:34:26,841
Just trust me.

625
00:34:26,865 --> 00:34:27,842
- Please.
- Mr. Matlock?

626
00:34:27,866 --> 00:34:30,244
Uh... right there, Your Honor.

627
00:34:30,268 --> 00:34:31,846
Mr. Matlock?

628
00:34:31,870 --> 00:34:39,720
Um... Uh, Your Honor?

629
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:43,624
Uh, defense would like
to re... request a recess

630
00:34:43,648 --> 00:34:45,393
until tomorrow morning.

631
00:34:45,417 --> 00:34:47,261
In the middle of counsel's
cross-examination?

632
00:34:47,285 --> 00:34:48,412
May I ask why?

633
00:34:49,621 --> 00:34:51,299
Uh, yes, sir.

634
00:34:51,323 --> 00:34:53,000
Your Honor, I-I ate

635
00:34:53,024 --> 00:34:56,003
one of those fat
California hot dogs

636
00:34:56,027 --> 00:34:58,039
with some real
strong onions on it,

637
00:34:58,063 --> 00:34:59,373
and they're kind of
coming back on me.

638
00:34:59,397 --> 00:35:00,641
Maybe you noticed?

639
00:35:00,665 --> 00:35:04,193
This, uh, court is adjourned
till 9:00 a.m. tomorrow.

640
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:12,119
Why did I do that?

641
00:35:12,143 --> 00:35:13,254
Because I asked you to.

642
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:14,922
That's so sweet of you.

643
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:17,458
Are you going to tell me
why you asked me to do that?

644
00:35:17,482 --> 00:35:18,793
I can't tell you right now.

645
00:35:18,817 --> 00:35:20,094
I'll tell you later.

646
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:22,196
But meet me at
your hotel at 6:00.

647
00:35:22,220 --> 00:35:24,815
Promise.

648
00:35:28,093 --> 00:35:30,471
I really don't want to have
this conversation with you.

649
00:35:30,495 --> 00:35:32,039
Well, then, why are we here?

650
00:35:32,063 --> 00:35:34,475
Even now, you won't
admit it, will you?

651
00:35:34,499 --> 00:35:35,810
What?

652
00:35:35,834 --> 00:35:37,878
You were at Peter's on
the night of the murder.

653
00:35:41,272 --> 00:35:43,117
The crystal elephant, Jackie...

654
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,019
The one that
Catherine gave Peter,

655
00:35:45,043 --> 00:35:46,554
the one the police
couldn't find...

656
00:35:46,578 --> 00:35:47,888
It's in your den.

657
00:35:47,912 --> 00:35:51,258
You lied. You lied to
me. You lied to Ben.

658
00:35:51,282 --> 00:35:52,460
You lied to your sister.

659
00:35:52,484 --> 00:35:53,995
You can't believe I killed him.

660
00:35:54,019 --> 00:35:55,630
What's going on?

661
00:35:55,654 --> 00:35:59,033
Well, I went to Peter's
house to offer him $100,000

662
00:35:59,057 --> 00:36:00,735
for those pictures of Catherine.

663
00:36:00,759 --> 00:36:02,937
Since-Since all he
wanted was money,

664
00:36:02,961 --> 00:36:04,205
I thought he'd grab it.

665
00:36:04,229 --> 00:36:06,173
And he would have.

666
00:36:06,197 --> 00:36:09,343
But he was dead
when I got there.

667
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:11,312
You must believe me!

668
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:14,181
When I saw him, I
panicked and I ran!

669
00:36:14,205 --> 00:36:15,449
What about the elephant?

670
00:36:15,473 --> 00:36:17,551
Well, it was there
sitting in a box

671
00:36:17,575 --> 00:36:18,953
with a note from Catherine.

672
00:36:18,977 --> 00:36:22,890
I-I took it so-so I
could protect her.

673
00:36:22,914 --> 00:36:26,260
Why didn't you tell
Catherine you were there?

674
00:36:26,284 --> 00:36:30,016
Because I don't know
whether she killed Peter or not.

675
00:36:43,234 --> 00:36:44,345
I'm sorry I'm late.

676
00:36:44,369 --> 00:36:45,680
The freeway is a parking lot.

677
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:47,114
Will you tell me
what's going on?

678
00:36:47,138 --> 00:36:49,684
It was Jackie who was
at Peter Bates' house

679
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:51,852
on the night of the
murder, not Catherine.

680
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:52,887
How do you know?

681
00:36:52,911 --> 00:36:53,935
Jackie...

682
00:36:56,448 --> 00:36:59,760
Jackie took the
crystal elephant.

683
00:36:59,784 --> 00:37:03,431
She took it home with
her, but she didn't kill Peter.

684
00:37:03,455 --> 00:37:05,099
Was she driving Catherine's car?

685
00:37:05,123 --> 00:37:08,936
Yes. Jackie had loaned
her car to her secretary.

686
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:11,072
Catherine's car just
happened to be there,

687
00:37:11,096 --> 00:37:12,540
so Jackie borrowed it.

688
00:37:12,564 --> 00:37:14,842
She wanted to go to
Peter's to offer him money

689
00:37:14,866 --> 00:37:16,243
for the pictures,

690
00:37:16,267 --> 00:37:18,713
but when she got there,
he was already dead.

691
00:37:18,737 --> 00:37:21,215
Julie, I know that
Jackie's a friend of yours...

692
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:25,643
I know, but I believe her.

693
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:29,924
I've known her for
such a long time,

694
00:37:29,948 --> 00:37:32,493
I would know if she were lying.

695
00:37:32,517 --> 00:37:35,453
And she's telling the truth.

696
00:37:37,322 --> 00:37:42,336
Well, if that's so, then
it must be Gil Altman.

697
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:44,939
I'm gonna
double-check his alibi.

698
00:37:44,963 --> 00:37:50,010
I would. What I don't get is if
Gil Altman killed Peter Bates,

699
00:37:50,034 --> 00:37:53,198
why'd he steal
Catherine's makeup?

700
00:38:04,082 --> 00:38:06,594
<i>You know a lot of
good-lookin' women.</i>

701
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:09,530
Ah, yes, I do.

702
00:38:09,554 --> 00:38:12,266
What, did you come here
to talk about celebrities?

703
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:16,537
No, no, I came to
talk about the, uh,

704
00:38:16,561 --> 00:38:17,671
the night of the murder.

705
00:38:17,695 --> 00:38:20,274
Oh, I-I thought we
already discussed that.

706
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:23,277
Well, uh, you gave
a barbecue that night.

707
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:24,678
- Mm-hmm, yeah.
- I talked to

708
00:38:24,702 --> 00:38:26,981
your guests, and they said
they had a wonderful time,

709
00:38:27,005 --> 00:38:30,117
but that you left your
own party for over an hour.

710
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:32,219
That's what this is all about.

711
00:38:32,243 --> 00:38:34,221
I ran out of propane
gas for the barbecue,

712
00:38:34,245 --> 00:38:36,791
and I had to have
my tank refilled.

713
00:38:36,815 --> 00:38:39,727
Oh... You remember where
you took your tank to be filled?

714
00:38:39,751 --> 00:38:41,562
Sure, I'll... I'll write
it down for you.

715
00:38:41,586 --> 00:38:42,586
Okay.

716
00:38:44,823 --> 00:38:46,621
It should be right here.

717
00:38:50,628 --> 00:38:55,464
Uh, are those the pictures of
Catherine that Peter Bates took?

718
00:38:57,001 --> 00:38:59,947
Uh, yeah. Yeah, they are.

719
00:38:59,971 --> 00:39:01,949
Uh... let me see.

720
00:39:01,973 --> 00:39:04,033
Ah, there it is.

721
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:11,592
On the night Peter
Bates was killed,

722
00:39:11,616 --> 00:39:16,530
you had some friends
over, uh, for a barbecue.

723
00:39:16,554 --> 00:39:18,532
- That right?
- Yes.

724
00:39:18,556 --> 00:39:20,901
But somewhere around 6:00,

725
00:39:20,925 --> 00:39:23,170
you left your house
for around an hour.

726
00:39:23,194 --> 00:39:24,505
As I told you earlier,

727
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:26,874
I ran out of propane
gas for my barbecue,

728
00:39:26,898 --> 00:39:29,443
- and I went out to have the tank refilled.
- That's right.

729
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:32,980
This is the receipt
from Phil's Truck Rental.

730
00:39:33,004 --> 00:39:36,050
Now, you have a standard,
uh, ten-pound tank?

731
00:39:36,074 --> 00:39:37,484
Yes, I do.

732
00:39:37,508 --> 00:39:40,054
Well, look here,
when they filled it,

733
00:39:40,078 --> 00:39:42,857
they could only
get in two pounds.

734
00:39:42,881 --> 00:39:45,192
You had eight pounds
of propane in that tank

735
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:46,360
when you came in there.

736
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:47,828
That's enough to cook hamburgers

737
00:39:47,852 --> 00:39:49,830
for this whole
courtroom, maybe more.

738
00:39:49,854 --> 00:39:51,565
Maybe the tank
wasn't hooked up right.

739
00:39:51,589 --> 00:39:52,867
I-I wasn't getting anything.

740
00:39:52,891 --> 00:39:54,568
Oh, it was hooked up right.

741
00:39:54,592 --> 00:39:56,837
You just needed an excuse

742
00:39:56,861 --> 00:39:59,540
to leave your house, go
to Peter Bates's house,

743
00:39:59,564 --> 00:40:03,077
kill him, and come back
without arousing suspicion.

744
00:40:04,469 --> 00:40:06,180
What, are you crazy?!

745
00:40:06,204 --> 00:40:08,716
You know I'm not crazy.

746
00:40:08,740 --> 00:40:14,288
Now, besides that
nearly full propane tank,

747
00:40:14,312 --> 00:40:18,192
this is People's Exhibit 27:

748
00:40:18,216 --> 00:40:20,828
Catherine Welden's makeup kit.

749
00:40:20,852 --> 00:40:23,964
It was found at the
scene of the crime

750
00:40:23,988 --> 00:40:25,232
the night of the murder.

751
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:28,335
As you can see, it
has six items in it.

752
00:40:28,359 --> 00:40:30,170
Yeah, that's, that's
very interesting.

753
00:40:30,194 --> 00:40:34,508
Catherine tells me the kit that
she left at Peter Bates' house

754
00:40:34,532 --> 00:40:37,645
the night <i>before</i> the
murder had seven items in it.

755
00:40:37,669 --> 00:40:39,046
Catherine should know.

756
00:40:39,070 --> 00:40:40,714
- She created the kit.
- Yeah.

757
00:40:40,738 --> 00:40:44,018
Where's the seventh
item, the concealer?

758
00:40:44,042 --> 00:40:45,219
I don't know.

759
00:40:45,243 --> 00:40:46,820
Your guess is as good as mine.

760
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:48,589
You know what a concealer is?

761
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:50,190
Yes, it's used for...

762
00:40:50,214 --> 00:40:52,059
It's used to cover something.

763
00:40:52,083 --> 00:40:56,397
To conceal a blemish,
a mark, a black eye.

764
00:40:56,421 --> 00:41:00,200
I'm sure all killers
hope for a quick kill,

765
00:41:00,224 --> 00:41:01,402
i-immediate death.

766
00:41:01,426 --> 00:41:03,604
But I'm also sure that
sometimes the gun

767
00:41:03,628 --> 00:41:06,140
or the poker or the knife

768
00:41:06,164 --> 00:41:09,710
misses that crucial
spot just an instant,

769
00:41:09,734 --> 00:41:12,479
giving the victim
time to strike out!

770
00:41:12,503 --> 00:41:14,648
Maybe that's what happened
to you when you stabbed

771
00:41:14,672 --> 00:41:18,052
Peter Bates... he lived just
long enough to strike out!

772
00:41:18,076 --> 00:41:20,054
And the result was a black eye.

773
00:41:20,078 --> 00:41:22,890
And you couldn't go home to
your friends with a black eye.

774
00:41:22,914 --> 00:41:24,291
"Where'd you
get it?" they'd say.

775
00:41:24,315 --> 00:41:27,528
And there it was, right in
front of you in the living room...

776
00:41:27,552 --> 00:41:29,830
Her concealer.

777
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:33,267
With that, you could go
home with no questions asked.

778
00:41:33,291 --> 00:41:35,803
Objection: speculation.

779
00:41:35,827 --> 00:41:36,804
Sustained.

780
00:41:36,828 --> 00:41:38,238
That's what happened, isn't it?

781
00:41:38,262 --> 00:41:39,673
- Mr. Matlock?
- I went

782
00:41:39,697 --> 00:41:42,676
from my house to
Phil's Truck Rentals

783
00:41:42,700 --> 00:41:45,033
and back to my house.

784
00:41:46,804 --> 00:41:51,986
You know, I didn't know
much about makeup

785
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:54,955
till I got involved
in this case.

786
00:41:54,979 --> 00:41:59,760
Did you know that a
lot of people are allergic

787
00:41:59,784 --> 00:42:01,895
to certain makeups?

788
00:42:01,919 --> 00:42:04,131
No. I...

789
00:42:04,155 --> 00:42:08,135
Uh, would you
tell me, Mr. Altman,

790
00:42:08,159 --> 00:42:11,596
who Dr. Seymour Weinstock is?

791
00:42:13,231 --> 00:42:16,043
He's... he's... he's
my, uh, dermatologist.

792
00:42:16,067 --> 00:42:17,711
When'd you see
him last? Remember?

793
00:42:17,735 --> 00:42:20,114
I... no, I... I don't remember.

794
00:42:20,138 --> 00:42:25,452
You saw him two days
after Peter Bates was killed.

795
00:42:25,476 --> 00:42:27,721
Do you know why you saw him?

796
00:42:27,745 --> 00:42:32,192
Uh, oh, yeah, there...
I do remember why.

797
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:33,761
I-I had a rash...

798
00:42:33,785 --> 00:42:35,829
A rash or an allergic
reaction to something?

799
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:37,831
- A rash.
- A rash.

800
00:42:37,855 --> 00:42:43,003
So you put <i>more</i>
makeup on this "rash."

801
00:42:43,027 --> 00:42:48,175
Probably a different kind,
because no one noticed it,

802
00:42:48,199 --> 00:42:49,843
not even your wife.

803
00:42:49,867 --> 00:42:51,678
Objection! Your
Honor, Mr. Matlock

804
00:42:51,702 --> 00:42:53,847
is engaging in
rampant speculation

805
00:42:53,871 --> 00:42:55,582
and then offering up hearsay

806
00:42:55,606 --> 00:42:57,885
to support his
unfounded allegations.

807
00:42:57,909 --> 00:42:59,086
Sustained.

808
00:42:59,110 --> 00:43:03,775
I never went to
Peter Bates's house.

809
00:43:06,684 --> 00:43:08,729
You know Julie March?

810
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:10,097
Yes, of course I do.

811
00:43:10,121 --> 00:43:12,199
You remember, she
came by your office

812
00:43:12,223 --> 00:43:14,802
a couple days after
Peter Bates was killed?

813
00:43:14,826 --> 00:43:16,837
- Yes, I remember the visit.
- You remember

814
00:43:16,861 --> 00:43:19,339
while you were talking with her,

815
00:43:19,363 --> 00:43:22,843
you tore up those awful
photos of Catherine,

816
00:43:22,867 --> 00:43:26,914
those pictures that Peter was
gonna use to blackmail her with.

817
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:28,082
Of course I tore them up.

818
00:43:28,106 --> 00:43:30,050
My job is to protect Ms. Welden.

819
00:43:30,074 --> 00:43:33,854
Yeah. You know, the other day...

820
00:43:33,878 --> 00:43:39,626
I found <i>this</i> set of
pictures at your house.

821
00:43:39,650 --> 00:43:42,796
I'll just show them to you.

822
00:43:42,820 --> 00:43:43,797
See?

823
00:43:43,821 --> 00:43:45,966
Where'd you get 'em?

824
00:43:45,990 --> 00:43:47,835
From Peter Bates, I suppose.

825
00:43:47,859 --> 00:43:51,572
But he only made up
four sets of these pictures.

826
00:43:51,596 --> 00:43:56,510
He gave one to Jackie
Flemming, one to Edgar Welden.

827
00:43:56,534 --> 00:43:59,580
He kept one, gave you
one that you tore up.

828
00:43:59,604 --> 00:44:01,515
So I ask you again,
where'd you get these?

829
00:44:01,539 --> 00:44:05,252
Maybe you found 'em
at Peter Bates's house

830
00:44:05,276 --> 00:44:06,720
after you killed him.

831
00:44:06,744 --> 00:44:08,255
But you couldn't
leave 'em there.

832
00:44:08,279 --> 00:44:10,591
What if somebody saw 'em?

833
00:44:10,615 --> 00:44:11,992
Couldn't have that.

834
00:44:12,016 --> 00:44:16,029
Catherine Welden paid you
a lot of money to protect her.

835
00:44:16,053 --> 00:44:18,098
And so that's what
you did, you took them.

836
00:44:18,122 --> 00:44:20,167
- Object!
- For what it's worth,

837
00:44:20,191 --> 00:44:22,302
I don't think you framed
Catherine on purpose.

838
00:44:22,326 --> 00:44:24,872
But when she was arrested,
you didn't come forward!

839
00:44:24,896 --> 00:44:27,040
And money's one thing,
and murder charge is

840
00:44:27,064 --> 00:44:28,642
- something else entirely!
- Object!

841
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:31,311
Your Honor,
objection! Speculation!

842
00:44:31,335 --> 00:44:32,335
Sustained.

843
00:44:36,941 --> 00:44:38,967
Speculation?

844
00:44:43,314 --> 00:44:45,306
Let me say this...

845
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:50,564
I'm sure you'll
have to admit, sir...

846
00:44:50,588 --> 00:44:52,580
and you...

847
00:44:55,459 --> 00:44:57,360
and you...

848
00:44:59,163 --> 00:45:03,277
that his leaving his house
for an hour, maybe more...

849
00:45:03,301 --> 00:45:08,315
that nearly full
tank of propane...

850
00:45:08,339 --> 00:45:11,785
the missing concealer,
the rash, more makeup,

851
00:45:11,809 --> 00:45:13,587
the set of pictures

852
00:45:13,611 --> 00:45:17,624
that only Peter Bates
should have had...

853
00:45:17,648 --> 00:45:22,129
casts more than a shadow
of doubt that my client

854
00:45:22,153 --> 00:45:26,523
could have in any way
committed this murder.

855
00:45:28,726 --> 00:45:32,720
I wish you all good
caution in your decision.

856
00:45:36,300 --> 00:45:37,377
We find the defendant,

857
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:39,927
Catherine Welden, not guilty.

858
00:45:50,848 --> 00:45:52,793
Fellas, now come
on. Give us a break.

859
00:45:52,817 --> 00:45:55,062
All the pictures you
want downstairs, all right?

860
00:45:55,086 --> 00:45:56,463
Come on. Knock it off.

861
00:45:56,487 --> 00:45:58,966
Julie, I can't thank you enough.

862
00:45:58,990 --> 00:46:01,735
I decided to tell
Catherine everything.

863
00:46:01,759 --> 00:46:03,370
Good. Make a clean slate of it.

864
00:46:03,394 --> 00:46:04,571
I will.

865
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:06,440
Ben's offered to take
us all out for dinner.

866
00:46:06,464 --> 00:46:08,008
- Oh, great.
- Great! Where?

867
00:46:08,032 --> 00:46:09,977
Well, it's your
town, you name it.

868
00:46:10,001 --> 00:46:12,312
I must warn you, I have
very expensive taste.

869
00:46:12,336 --> 00:46:13,347
What's money for?

870
00:46:13,371 --> 00:46:15,349
Oh, lucky you!

871
00:46:15,373 --> 00:46:18,775
I'm gonna save this receipt
and write this sucker off.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
